<title>USA: Atria to acquire American ElderServe.</title>
<headline>Atria to acquire American ElderServe.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atria Communities Inc said on Tuesday it has agreed to acquire American ElderServe Corp for stock, cash and the assumption of debt in a deal valued at $30 million.</p>
<p>American ElderServe, based in Atlanta, operates 12 assisted-living communities and has six more scheduled to open this year. Atria operates 23 communities in 13 states.</p>
<p>American ElderServe's current president and chief executive, Andrew Schoepf, joins Atria as chief operating officer effective March 13.</p>
</text>
